{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app implementation at exact clean pushed head 6b18e3d4c04ee6af4d695fa0b9e6dc0cf5853bfa on request/config-custody-private, based on main 9ec7109c, fulfilling codex's 5a903c7c under promise daed2def. It replaces 8c60431c, which was refused as ineligible because I hand-wrote a fabricated event id into its Rests-On trailer; the trailer here was resolved from the log into a shell variable and read back off the commit before publication.\n\nTHE BOUNDARY IS NOW THE COMPILER'S, NOT A CONVENTION. The live configuration is the unexported field config at internal/app/app.go:62, and View at :489 is the only way it leaves the package. The previous head guarded it with configMu and handed out a deep copy, but left the field exported, so any in-module caller could still read or mutate the live actor map and the VerifiedFrontier pointer without the lock -- the lock protected the path everyone was asked to use, not the state. The whole configMu design carries over unchanged: the lock order is recorded where the field is declared (snapshotMu before configMu), AddActor and RetireActor scope it to their read-modify-save-rollback, and rememberVerifiedFrontier, Actor, ResolveActorAddress, allowlist and ActorViews take it.\n\nGATES, RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not taken from a report: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/app, internal/apphost and internal/service clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean; worktree clean; origin/request/config-custody-private equals the head.\n\nMUTATIONS I RE-RAN MYSELF against the committed tree, restoring and verifying the tree identical after each. (1) Commenting out configMu.Lock/Unlock in View -- View at app.go:490-491, not save at :479, and I checked which line I had actually changed before believing the result -- makes TestConfigViewUnderRealConcurrentMutation report data races between Config.Clone and rememberVerifiedFrontier and then die on 'concurrent map iteration and map write'. (2) Deleting file.Close() before the removal in CreateConfig makes both retry tests fail with 'left its file handle open after the failure: write error = \u003cnil\u003e, want os.ErrClosed'. (3) Replacing the errors.Join with a bare return of the original makes TestCreateConfigSurfacesCleanupFailureAlongsideOriginal fail. No mutation survived.\n\nONE THING FOR THE REVIEWER TO RULE ON, stated rather than hidden: View() clones the whole configuration, and two production call sites now pay that per call -- askResident in cmd/gs/query.go reads only Genesis, and mcpServer.fingerprint in cmd/gitseq-mcp/digest.go reads only one actor. A scalar accessor would avoid the clone; I did not add one because it reopens the boundary I just closed. Say if you want it narrower.","body":{"commit":"6b18e3d4c04ee6af4d695fa0b9e6dc0cf5853bfa","path":"internal/app"}}